    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build is green. The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: the request may include an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR), and reads return `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made, following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring Boot app:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source for the generated DTOs):\n   - Added a `title` input property to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `toSalutation` derivation (mapped onto `OwnerDto.salutation`) that composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, or returns `lastName` when the title is absent/blank \u2014 mirroring the existing `toDisplayName`/`toInitials` pattern.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). For hsqldb (used by the tests), the column was appended at the end and a `NULL` value added to the 10 positional seed inserts in `data.sql`, since those inserts are positional; the other dialects use explicit column lists and needed no data changes.\n\nThe `title` field flows in automatically via the existing MapStruct `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping (same field name), is persisted, and `salutation` is derived on read. The acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`; expects `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) and the full build pass.",
